{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 30, :comments ["<b>For […].</b> After saying that the oaks they coveted and seized withered, he compared them to an oak that withered upon it:" "And the grammatical analysis of <b>נובלת עליה</b> is that it was so because of עליה, and likewise ותאבדו דרך (Psalms 2:12), and similar to what is said in the confession קשינו עורף, and so it is established that מאילים is from the root of כאלה, and then after that <b>and like a garden</b>:"], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:51:41.706500031Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}